eues for a process","By increasing the waiting time","By giving each process a fixed time quantum","By allowing a process to move between queues"],"correct_answer":"By allowing a process to move between queues","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":253,"content":{"question":"What are the characteristics of Little''s Formula (n = λ x W)?","options":["In steady state, the number of processes leaving the queue equals the number of processes arriving","It is valid for any scheduling algorithm","It is valid for any arrival distribution","It can calculate CPU utilization"],"correct_answer":"In steady state, the number of processes leaving the queue equals the number of processes arriving\nIt is valid for any scheduling algorithm\nIt is valid for any arrival distribution","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":254,"content":{"question":"In priority scheduling, what is the solution to the problem of ''starvation''?","options":["Aging","Setting all priorities to be the same","Increasing the time quantum"],"correct_answer":"Aging","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":258,"content":{"question":"Turnaround time is the total time from process submission to [__1__].(Please answer in lowercase English)","options":[],"correct_answer":"terminated","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":260,"content":{"question":"在Windows系統中，[__1__]優先權類別的執行緒無法被提升優先權。(請用小寫英文回答 字母間用_連接)","options":[],"correct_answer":"realtime_priority_class","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":261,"content":{"question":"The CPU-I/O burst cycle is a cycle of process execution where a CPU burst is followed by an [__1__] burst.(Please use uppercase English letters)","options":[],"correct_answer":"I/O","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":262,"content":{"question":"哪一個排程演算法被認為是最佳的，因為它能提供給定程序集的最小平均等待時間？","options":["短工作優先 (SJF)","先到先服務 (FCFS)","輪轉 (RR)","優先權排程"],"correct_answer":"短工作優先 (SJF)","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":263,"content":{"question":"The performance of Round Robin (RR) scheduling is related to which factors?","options":["The size of the time quantum (q)","The time of a context switch","The number of processes in the ready queue","The type of process (CPU-bound or I/O-bound)"],"correct_answer":"The size of the time quantum (q)\nThe time of a context switch\nThe number of processes in the ready queue","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":264,"content":{"question":"The advantage of the Shortest-Job-First (SJF) scheduling algorithm is that it minimizes the average [__1__] time.(Please answer in lowercase English)","options":[],"correct_answer":"waiting","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":265,"content":{"question":"When the time quantum (q) in Round Robin (RR) is very large, the algorithm''s behavior approaches which scheduling type?","options":["First-Come, First-Served (FCFS)","Shortest-Job-First (SJF)","Priority scheduling","Multilevel queue"],"correct_answer":"First-Come, First-Served (FCFS)","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":266,"content":{"question":"What are the characteristics of First-Come, First-Served (FCFS) scheduling?","options":["Simple and easy to understand","It can lead to the ''convoy effect''","The waiting time is always minimal","It is suitable for real-time systems"],"correct_answer":"Simple and easy to understand\nIt can lead to the ''convoy effect''","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":268,"content":{"question":"CPU [__1__] is the tendency of a process to run on the same processor.(Please answer in lowercase English)","options":[],"correct_answer":"affinity","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":269,"content":{"question":"In Solaris scheduling, how does the scheduler handle multiple threads with the same highest priority?","options":["It uses Round Robin scheduling","It uses preemptive scheduling","It selects one randomly","It selects based on their creation time"],"correct_answer":"It uses Round Robin scheduling","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":270,"content":{"question":"In scheduling algorithm evaluation, what method uses a predetermined workload to define the performance of each algorithm?","options":["Implementation","Simulations","Deterministic modeling","Queueing models"],"correct_answer":"Deterministic modeling","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":276,"content":{"question":"Which of the following scheduling decisions are nonpreemptive?","options":["A process switches from the running to the waiting state","A process terminates","A process switches from the running to the ready state","A process switches from the waiting to the ready state"],"correct_answer":"A process switches from the running to the waiting state\nA process terminates","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":278,"content":{"question":"In Windows, under what circumstances is a thread''s priority boosted?","options":["When it returns from a waiting state","When it is in the foreground window","When its quantum expires","When it is preempted by a higher-priority thread"],"correct_answer":"When it returns from a waiting state\nWhen it is in the foreground window","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":283,"content":{"question":"In non-preemptive scheduling, once the CPU has been allocated to a process, the process keeps the CPU until it [__1__] or [__2__].(Please answer in lowercase English)","options":[],"correct_answer":"terminated/released","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":285,"content":{"question":"What is the core objective of CPU scheduling?","options":["Minimize code complexity","Maximize I/O wait time","Decrease CPU utilization","Maximize CPU utilization"],"correct_answer":"Maximize CPU utilization","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":287,"content":{"question":"What type of scheduler is the CPU scheduler?","options":["Short-term scheduler","Long-term scheduler"],"correct_answer":"Short-term scheduler","type":"choice"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":288,"content":{"question":"After Linux kernel version 2.6.23, the scheduler picks the next task to run based on the lowest [__1__] value.(Please answer in lowercase English, leaving a space between each word)","options":[],"correct_answer":"vruntime","type":"fill_blank"}},{"subject_id":"os","unit_id":"u6","target_id":289,"content":{"question":"What methods can be used to estimate the length of the next CPU burst?","options":["Setting α=1 to only consider the last burst","Asking the user","Using exponential averaging of previous CPU bursts","Using a constant value"],"correct_answer":"Setting α=1 to only consider the last burst\nAsking the user\nUsing exponential averaging of previous CPU bursts","type":"choice"}}]'::jsonb) as x(subject_id text,unit_id text,target_id bigint,content jsonb) on conflict(subject_id,unit_id,target_id) do update set content=excluded.content;
